window.AG_CHAPTERS["14"] = {"id":"14","title":"Fire Above, Dryness Below","titleZh":"上面是火，下面是乾","patient":{"name":"Widow Cao 曹娘子","sprite":"girl"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-treatment.jpg","key":"rain"},"pattern":"Heart and Kidney Failing to Communicate 心腎不交","principle":"enrich yin, bring down empty fire, and let Heart and Kidney reach one another","tongue":"red body, red tip, scant coating","pulseNote":{"en":"Thin and hurrying, and thinnest of all under the ring finger.","zh":"細而數，尤以尺部為細"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>N&#232;igu&#257;n PC6</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"PC6","zh":"內關","py":"N&#232;igu&#257;n","x":201,"y":570,"img":"art/body-forearm-palmar.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"view":{"x":60,"y":400,"w":310,"h":400},"decoys":[{"x":140,"y":652},{"x":201,"y":611},{"x":185,"y":530},{"x":160,"y":158},{"x":230,"y":600}],"note":"<b>內關 N&#232;igu&#257;n PC6</b> — 2 cun above the wrist crease, between the tendons of palmaris longus and flexor carpi radialis. Connecting point of the Pericardium and confluent point of the Yin Wei mai; the principal point for palpitations and an unsettled spirit.<br>腕橫紋上二寸，掌長肌腱與橈側腕屈肌腱之間。心包絡穴，八脈交會通陰維。主心悸、安神。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Divide her complaints into the ones <b>above</b> the diaphragm and the ones <b>below</b> it. Then look at what each half is doing.","zh":"分其症為膈上、膈下二部。而後觀二部各為何狀。"},"look":{"en":"Look at the tip of the tongue in particular. It has its own correspondence.","zh":"尤當觀舌尖。其部自有所候。"},"pulse":{"en":"Feel the rear position under the ring finger. That is where the lower half of this case answers.","zh":"當察無名指下之尺部。本案下半，應於此處。"},"dx":{"en":"Name the two halves. Then decide which half is the root. Then say how this differs from the other Heart-and-Kidney pattern.","zh":"先名其上下二部，次定何者為本，末辨其與心腎另一證何異。"},"rx":{"en":"Settle the spirit above, and refill the water below. One prescription must reach both floors of the house.","zh":"上安其神，下滋其水。一方而及樓之二層。"},"tech":{"en":"Two halves in opposite states. Ask whether one technique can serve both — you have met this question once before.","zh":"二部之狀相反。當自問一法可否兼之——此問你曾遇過一次。"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen notices she is sitting very upright, and very still.","zh":"參師父見她端坐甚正，且一動不動。"},{"who":"patient","en":"Widow Cao presses two fingers to her breastbone and takes them away again.","zh":"曹娘子以二指按胸骨，旋即放下。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy sets down tea. She wraps both hands around it although the room is warm.","zh":"藥童奉茶。屋內不冷，她卻雙手抱盞。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"She has not slept a full night since the spring. Ask her what happens when she lies down.\"","zh":"「自入春以來，未曾整夜安睡。問她躺下之後如何。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"My chest gets hot and my heart races,\" she says. \"And my feet stay cold all night.\"","zh":"「胸中發熱，心跳得快，」她說，「腳卻整夜是涼的。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Hot above, cold and dry below, in one body. Say what has stopped happening between them.\"","zh":"「一身之中，上熱而下寒且乾。當言：其間何事已不復行？」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"cold_heat","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"cold_heat","dx":"excess_def","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"excess_def"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Water and Fire Must Meet","cardZh":"水火既濟 · 交通心腎","cardTxt":"Kidney water should rise to cool the Heart; Heart fire should descend to warm the Kidney. When the water runs low it cannot rise, the fire is left unchecked above, and the lower half goes cold and dry while the upper half burns. Fire above, dryness below — one body, two climates. Enrich the water and the traffic resumes.","herbId":"danzhuye","herbEn":"Lophatherum Leaf","herbZh":"淡竹葉","herbImg":"art/card-danzhuye.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Sweet, bland and cold, entering Heart, Stomach and Small Intestine. It clears Heart heat and leads it downward and out through the urine — the Heart and Small Intestine being an interior-exterior pair. It handles the fire above while other herbs refill the water below; on its own it would drain a patient who is already short."},"endings":{"three":["A month later Widow Cao sleeps through until the fifth watch. \"My feet are warm now,\" she says, as though that were the smaller news.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You saw that the fire above and the cold below were one illness, not two. Students treat the insomnia, the fire comes back by the new moon, and they never ask why the water was low.\"","一月後，曹娘子能一覺至五更。「腳現在是暖的，」她說，彷彿這才是小事。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你看出上火下寒本是一病而非二病。學生但治其失眠，月缺而火復，終不問水何以少。」"],"two":["She falls asleep more easily but still wakes in the small hours.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You cooled the top of the house. The well underneath it is still low.\"","入睡易了些，夜半仍醒。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你涼了樓上。樓下之井，水仍不足。」"],"one":["No change, and she looks more tired than when she arrived.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Two halves, in opposite states. Until you name both, you will treat one and worsen the other.\"","未見好轉，且較來時更倦。<br><b>參師父：</b>「上下二部，其狀相反。二者未並舉，則治其一而害其一。」"],"titles":["Widow Cao Sleeps Until Dawn","Widow Cao Falls Asleep Easier","Widow Cao Will Need Another Visit"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"You have seen two organs press, two organs feed, and two organs fail together. Now two that have stopped speaking.","cn":"你已見二臟相迫、相養、同衰。今則見二臟不相往來。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. Cao. I have not slept properly since spring. I lie down and my chest burns and my heart gallops.","cn":"大夫。姓曹。自春以來未得安睡。一躺下便胸中燔熱、心跳如奔。"},{"w":"patient","en":"And yet my feet are cold every night, and my back aches, and there is a ringing in my ears.","cn":"然雙足夜夜冰涼，腰痠，耳中亦鳴。"},{"w":"master","en":"Listen to the shape of that. Heat and racing above. Cold, ache and ringing below. In one body, at the same hour.","cn":"聽其形勢：上則熱而躁，下則寒、痠而鳴。同一身，同一時。"},{"w":"master","en":"Nothing invaded her. Something between the two halves has simply stopped.","cn":"非有邪犯之。乃上下之間，有一事已止。"}],"qa":[{"q":"What exactly happens when you lie down at night?","cq":"夜間就寢之後，究竟如何？","good":1,"a":"My chest and face get hot, my heart races, and my mind will not stop. When I do sleep I dream all night.","ca":"胸面發熱，心跳加快，思緒不止。睡著了也整夜作夢。","clue":{"en":"Night-time chest heat, racing heart, restless mind, dream-disturbed sleep","zh":"夜間胸中煩熱、心悸而數、心煩、多夢"},"note":"The upper half, and all of it is the Heart. The Heart governs the blood vessels and houses the spirit, so a Heart disturbed by heat gives palpitations <i>and</i> an unsettled mind together. Note the palpitations are <b>fast</b> — that will matter shortly. 此上部之症，皆屬心。心主血脈而藏神，故心為熱擾者，悸與煩並見。且其悸為數——此點稍後即為關鍵。"},{"q":"And below — the back, the knees, the water?","cq":"下部呢？腰、膝、小便如何？","good":1,"a":"My low back aches, my knees are weak, my ears ring, and my feet are cold at night.","ca":"腰痠、膝軟、耳鳴，夜間足冷。","clue":{"en":"Sore low back, weak knees, tinnitus, cold feet at night","zh":"腰痠膝軟、耳鳴、夜間足冷"},"note":"The lower half, and all of it is the Kidney — the low back is its house, it governs the bones and knees, and it opens into the ears. Two halves, two organs, one patient. 此下部之症，皆屬腎——腰為腎之府，主骨與膝，開竅於耳。二部、二臟、一人。"},{"q":"Do you have night sweats and heat in the palms and soles?","cq":"盜汗嗎？手足心熱嗎？","good":1,"a":"Yes, and a dry mouth at night. My throat is dry but I do not want to drink much.","ca":"有，夜間口乾。咽乾而不欲多飲。","clue":{"en":"Night sweats, five-centre heat, dry mouth without much thirst","zh":"盜汗、五心煩熱、口乾而不甚渴"},"note":"Empty heat confirmed, and it names the root. The heat above is not an invader — it is what happens when there is too little yin below to hold yang down. Dry mouth without real thirst is the classic marker of yin shortage rather than a hot pathogen. 虛熱既定，且指其本。上熱非外邪，乃下陰不足以潛陽之故。口乾而不甚渴，正陰虧之徵，非熱邪之象。"},{"q":"Is your heartbeat slow, and do your ankles swell?","cq":"心跳遲緩嗎？足踝浮腫嗎？","good":0,"a":"No, quite the opposite — it races. And nothing is swollen.","ca":"適反，跳得快。也無浮腫。","clue":"","note":"<b>The most important exclusion in the case.</b> A slow heartbeat with pitting oedema and cold limbs would be Heart-and-Kidney <i>yang</i> deficiency — the same two organs, the opposite mechanism, and the pattern most often confused with this one. Fast versus slow, and swelling versus none, separate them in one question. 本案最要之排除。心悸而遲、凹陷性水腫、肢冷者，心腎陽虛也：臟同而機反，最易與本證相混。遲數與腫否，一問即分。"},{"q":"Has anything changed in your circumstances?","cq":"境遇有何變化？","good":0,"a":"My husband died in the winter. But this began after, not before — I was sleeping until spring.","ca":"外子冬天走的。但此症起於其後，非其前——我睡到開春都還好。","clue":"","note":"Worth asking and worth hearing carefully. Grief and a long strain deplete yin over months, so the history fits — but she is right that the timing makes this a depletion that followed, not a constraint that started it. Kindly asked, it also tells you what the treatment has to hold. 問得其宜，聽亦當細。憂傷積月則耗陰，其史相合；然其言不誤：此為其後之虧，非其先之鬱。溫言問之，亦知所當扶者為何。"}],"look":[{"t":"Red body, redder at the tip, with scant coating","c":"舌紅、尖尤紅、少苔","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Red tongue with a redder tip, scant coat","zh":"舌紅、舌尖尤紅、苔少"},"note":"Correct, and the <b>tip</b> is the finding that makes it specific. The tongue is mapped: tip = Heart and upper burner, centre = Spleen and Stomach, root = Kidney, sides = Liver and Gallbladder. A generally red tongue says yin is short; a tip that is redder still says the fire is gathering at the top. Scant coat says the shortage is real. 是，而舌尖乃其確憑。舌分部候：尖候心與上焦，中候脾胃，根候腎，邊候肝膽。通體紅者陰虧，尖獨紅者火聚於上。少苔則其虧為實。"},{"t":"Pale swollen body, moist, with a white coat","c":"舌淡胖而潤、苔白","ok":0,"note":"Heart and Kidney <i>yang</i> deficiency — the look-alike pattern. Pale and wet versus red and dry is the whole distinction. 心腎陽虛之象，即其易混之證。淡潤與紅乾，別盡在此。"},{"t":"Red body with a thick yellow coat","c":"舌紅、苔黃厚","ok":0,"note":"Full heat with substance behind it. A thick coat needs fluid to grow it; she has none to spare. 實熱有形之象。厚苔賴津而生，本案津不足以供。"},{"t":"Pale body with a thin white coat","c":"舌淡苔薄白","ok":0,"note":"Blood or qi deficiency without heat. There is heat in this case and it is on the tongue. 血虛或氣虛而無熱。本案有熱，且已見於舌。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Thready and rapid, weakest at the rear position 細數，尺部尤弱","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Thready rapid pulse, weak chi","zh":"脈細數、尺弱"},"note":"Correct, and the position is what makes this pulse tell the whole story. <b>Thready</b>: yin does not fill the vessel. <b>Rapid</b>: empty heat. And the <b>chi</b> position under the ring finger is where the Kidney answers — its particular weakness says the shortage is at the bottom of the house, which is exactly where the fire above came from. 是，而其部位使此脈能述全案。細者陰不充其道，數者虛熱。尺部候腎，其獨弱者，言其虧在下——而上之火，正由此而生。"},{"t":"Deep, slow and weak 沉遲無力","ok":0,"note":"Heart and Kidney yang deficiency. Slow, not fast — and her heart is racing. 心腎陽虛之脈。遲而非數，而其心跳甚急。"},{"t":"Knotted or intermittent 結代","ok":0,"note":"That points at Heart yang failing or a serious organ weakness, and in a breathless swollen patient it needs proper medical assessment rather than a training exercise. Her pulse is regular. 此主心陽衰或臟氣虛損；若兼喘促浮腫，當就正規醫療評估，非練習之事。本案脈律齊。"},{"t":"Wiry and rapid 弦數","ok":0,"note":"Liver fire — a red-faced, angry, bitter-mouthed patient with a forceful pulse. Hers is thin and gives way. 肝火之脈：面赤、易怒、口苦而脈有力。本案細而無力。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — name the two halves.<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：上下二部，各為何狀？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Fire above in the Heart, emptiness and cold below in the Kidney","c":"上焦心火，下焦腎虛而寒","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and sorting the case this way is the whole method here. <b>Above:</b> chest heat, racing heart, restless mind, dreaming, red tongue tip. <b>Below:</b> sore low back, weak knees, tinnitus, cold feet, weak chi pulse. Neither list explains the other on its own, and the patient feels both at the same hour of the same night. 是，此案之法，正在如此分之。上：胸中煩熱、心悸而數、心煩、多夢、舌尖紅。下：腰痠膝軟、耳鳴、足冷、尺脈弱。二者互不能相釋，而其人同夜同時並受之。"},{"t":"Fire above and fire below","c":"上下俱火","ok":0,"note":"Then her feet would not be cold and her chi pulse would not be weak. Half the findings would have nowhere to live. 若上下俱火，則足不當冷，尺脈不當弱。其症半數無處安放。"},{"t":"Cold above and heat below","c":"上寒下熱","ok":0,"note":"Reversed. The heat is in the chest and the face; the cold is in the feet. 顛倒矣。熱在胸面，寒在雙足。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — which half is the root?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：二部之中，何者為本？</small>","opts":[{"t":"The Kidney below — its yin is too low to rise and cool the Heart","c":"下之腎陰不足，不能上濟於心","ok":1,"note":"<b>The mechanism the chapter exists to teach.</b> Kidney water should rise to cool the Heart; Heart fire should descend to warm the Kidney — 水火既濟, water and fire completing each other. When the water runs low it cannot rise, so the fire above is left with nothing to check it and blazes, while the bottom of the house goes cold and dry. The fire is loud and the shortage is quiet, which is why students treat the wrong half. 本章所欲授之機。腎水當上濟以涼心，心火當下降以溫腎，是謂水火既濟。水虧則不能上，火失所制而上炎，而下部遂寒且乾。火顯而虧隱，故學生每治其非。"},{"t":"The Heart above — its fire is excessive and burns downward","c":"上之心火過旺，下灼於腎","ok":0,"note":"Tempting, because the fire is the loud half. But a truly excess Heart fire gives a forceful rapid pulse, a red face all day, mouth ulcers and constipation — and it does not leave the feet cold. Her pulse is thin and her chi is weak: this fire has no fuel behind it. 火為顯者，故易惑。然心火之實者，脈當數而有力、終日面赤、口舌生瘡、便秘，且不致足冷。本案脈細而尺弱：其火無所憑而然。"},{"t":"Neither — they are independent illnesses","c":"二者無涉，各為一病","ok":0,"note":"Then they would not have started together, worsen together, and ease together. And treating them as two would mean cooling a woman whose lower half is already cold. 若各為一病，則不當同起、同劇、同緩。且分而治之，則其下本寒而更涼之。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — how does this differ from Heart and Kidney yang deficiency?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：此與心腎陽虛何別？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Three axes: fast heart not slow, no oedema, heat not cold","c":"三軸可辨：心悸數而不遲、無水腫、熱而不寒","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and these two are the most confusable pair in the whole system because they name the same two organs. Learn the three axes as a unit. <b>This pattern:</b> yin deficient, palpitations fast, no swelling, five-centre heat, night sweats, red tongue with scant coat, thready rapid pulse. <b>Yang deficiency:</b> palpitations slow, pitting oedema, cold limbs throughout, pale wet tongue, deep slow weak pulse. Same two organs, opposite halves. 是。二證同舉二臟，故為全系最易混之對。三軸宜並記。本證屬陰虛：悸數、無腫、五心煩熱、盜汗、舌紅少苔、脈細數。陽虛則：悸遲、凹陷性水腫、通身肢冷、舌淡潤、脈沉遲無力。臟同而半反。"},{"t":"There is no meaningful difference","c":"二者無實質之別","ok":0,"note":"Then you would warm a woman whose chest is already burning, or cool a man whose feet are already blue. The two demand opposite treatments. 若然，則於胸中已燔者而溫之，於足已青者而涼之。二者所治適反。"},{"t":"This one involves the Liver as well","c":"此證兼及肝","ok":0,"note":"The Liver may well be involved in a long depletion, but that is not what separates these two patterns. The separating axis is yin versus yang. 久虧誠可及肝，然此非二證之別。所別者，陰陽耳。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"PC6","t":"N&#232;igu&#257;n PC6 內關","ok":1,"note":"Connecting point of the Pericardium and confluent point of the Yin Wei mai. The Pericardium shields the Heart, so this settles palpitations and an unsettled spirit without attacking the Heart itself — the right weight of hand for a patient this depleted. 心包絡穴，八脈交會通陰維。心包為心之外衛，故能定悸安神而不直攻其心——於大虛之人，手宜如此。"},{"id":"KI3","t":"T&#224;ix&#299; KI3 太谿","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Kidney, and here it refills the water that should be rising. This is the half students skip, because the fire above is louder — but without it the fire returns. 腎之原穴，於此所以實其當升之水。此半學生每略之，以上火之顯故；然不為此，其火必復。"},{"id":"SP6","t":"S&#257;ny&#299;nji&#257;o SP6 三陰交","ok":1,"note":"Where the three leg yin channels cross — one needle nourishing yin on three fronts, which is why it appears in almost every prescription for a yin-deficient patient who cannot sleep. 足三陰交會之處，一針而三陰俱滋。陰虛不寐之方，鮮有無此穴者。"},{"id":"LI4","t":"H&#233;g&#468; LI4 合谷","ok":0,"note":"Releases the exterior and moves qi strongly. No exterior pattern, and strong movement disperses fluids she cannot spare. 解表行氣力強。本案無表證，且強行則散其所不能失之津。"},{"id":"ST40","t":"F&#275;ngl&#243;ng ST40 豐隆","ok":0,"note":"Transforms phlegm and is drying by nature. There is no phlegm here, and drying is the wrong direction entirely. 化痰而性燥。本案無痰，且燥之適為其反。"},{"id":"GB34","t":"Y&#225;ngl&#237;ngqu&#225;n GB34 陽陵泉","ok":0,"note":"Sea point of the Gallbladder, for rib-side pain and sinew problems. That was chapter eleven's territory; nothing here points at the Liver or the sinews. 膽之合穴，主脅痛與筋病。此第十一章之事，本案不涉肝與筋。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reinforce the Kidney points and drain or even-method the Heart point","c":"腎穴用補，心（包）穴瀉之或平補平瀉","ok":1,"note":"<b>Correct, and it is the same shape of answer as chapter eleven for a completely different reason.</b> There, one organ was full and one empty. Here the whole patient is depleted, but the <i>fire above</i> still needs bringing down while the <i>water below</i> needs filling — so the hand changes by location rather than by organ: reinforce at KI3 and SP6, and use an even or gently reducing hand at PC6. And no moxa: she is dry and running hot at night. 是，其形與第十一章同，而其故迥異。彼一實一虛；此則通身皆虛，然上火猶當降，下水猶當充，故手法隨部而異：太谿、三陰交用補，內關平補平瀉或微瀉。且不施灸：其人夜間燥而有熱。"},{"t":"Reinforce everything, with moxa, since she is depleted","c":"通案用補並施灸，以其大虛","ok":0,"note":"The tonifying instinct is right; the moxa is the trap, and adding warmth to a chest that burns at night makes the night worse. Emptiness does not automatically mean warm it — you learned that in chapter seven and it applies again. 欲補之念不誤，而灸則其陷。其胸夜燔而更溫之，夜必更甚。虛者未必宜溫——此第七章所學，於此復用。"},{"t":"Drain everything, to clear the fire","c":"通案用瀉，以清其火","ok":0,"note":"Then you drain a woman whose lower half is already empty and cold. The fire is empty fire; draining it takes the last of her substance and it returns worse. 若然，則於下部已虛且寒者而瀉之。其火為虛火，瀉之則奪其僅存，火反更甚。"},{"t":"Reducing method throughout, since her heart is racing","c":"通案用瀉，以其心悸而數","ok":0,"note":"Fast is not the same as full. A racing heart in a depleted patient is the pulse of emptiness, not of excess — read the force, not the speed. 數不等於實。虛人心悸而數者，虛之脈也，非實之脈。當察其勢，不徒察其數。"}]};
